# Android push notifications, vendor services, and connectivity checks.
#
# These must stay DIRECT: routing them through a tunnel adds delivery latency,
# and when the VPN drops notifications stop arriving or the OS reports "no internet".
# Android / Google FCM
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,mtalk.google.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,mtalk4.google.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,alt1-mtalk.google.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,alt2-mtalk.google.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,alt3-mtalk.google.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,alt4-mtalk.google.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,alt5-mtalk.google.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,alt6-mtalk.google.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,alt7-mtalk.google.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,alt8-mtalk.google.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,android.clients.google.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,device-provisioning.googleapis.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,fcm.googleapis.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,firebaseinstallations.googleapis.com
# Android Connectivity & Captive Portal checks
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,connectivitycheck.gstatic.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,connectivitycheck.android.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,clients3.google.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,time.android.com
# Android Vendor Push & Captive Portal (Xiaomi, Huawei, Samsung)
